  "note": "Independent re-judgment against RFC 7911 Section 2 (\"However, the Path Identifier MUST be assigned in such a way that the BGP speaker is able to use the (Prefix, Path Identifier) to uniquely identify a path advertised to a neighbor.\"). Re-read tagged units TestForwardPathIDsDifferForCollidingSources and TestForwardPathIDStableAcrossUpdates plus diffs since fc9391009c across all 29 cited producer functions in adj_rib_out.go, forward_path_id.go, forward_provenance_withdraw.go, session_ownership.go, session_ownership_walk.go, session_rfc7607.go, and session_write.go. Test edits only supplied fwdPathIDFixtureOrigin(wire) to buildFwdBody; assertions on distinct local IDs for colliding sources and stability across repeated updates are unchanged. Producer updates strengthened source scoping (fwdPathSource keyed by {sourceID, peerOwner}), unlocked remote retention checks in releasePath with invalidating claim pointers, and added owner-keyed adjOutSelected/sourceOwner tracking without relaxing (Prefix, Path Identifier) uniqueness. All 29 producer keys remain present. Verdict unchanged: enforced.",
